{"tool_name":"rsem","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","debian","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"rsem","version":"1.3.3","home":"https://deweylab.github.io/RSEM","documentation":"https://deweylab.github.io/RSEM","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"RSEM is a software package for estimating gene and isoform expression levels from RNA-Seq data.","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/1471-2105-12-323","biotools:rsem"],"description":"\"RSEM is a software package for estimating gene and isoform expression levels from RNA-Seq data. \"\n\"The RSEM package provides an user-friendly interface, supports threads for parallel computation \"\n\"of the EM algorithm, single-end and paired-end read data, quality scores, variable-length reads \"\n\"and RSPD estimation. In addition, it provides posterior mean and 95% credibility interval \"\n\"estimates for expression levels. For visualization, It can generate BAM and Wiggle files in both \"\n\"transcript-coordinate and genomic-coordinate. Genomic-coordinate files can be visualized by both \"\n\"UCSC Genome browser and Broad Institute's Integrative Genomics Viewer (IGV). Transcript-coordinate \"\n\"files can be visualized by IGV. RSEM also has its own scripts to generate transcript read depth \"\n\"plots in pdf format. The unique feature of RSEM is, the read depth plots can be stacked, with read \"\n\"depth contributed to unique reads shown in black and contributed to multi-reads shown in red. In \"\n\"addition, models learned from data can also be visualized. Last but not least, RSEM contains a \"\n\"simulator.\"\n","license_file":"COPYING","build":{"number":12,"rpaths":["lib/R/lib/","lib/"],"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":["make",null],"host":["perl","perl-module-build","htslib","zlib"],"run":["bioconductor-biobase","bioconductor-ebseq","ucsc-bigwigsummary","perl","perl-module-build","r-base","samtools","htslib"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/deweylab/RSEM/archive/v1.3.3.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["rsem-prepare-reference 2>&1 | grep reference_name > /dev/null","rsem-for-ebseq-find-DE 2>&1 | grep Usage > /dev/null","rsem-bam2wig foo bar foobar 2>&1 | grep \"Failed to open file\" > /dev/null","which rsem-for-ebseq-calculate-clustering-info \u00a0# [not aarch64]","test -x ${PREFIX}/bin/rsem-for-ebseq-calculate-clustering-info"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"rsem","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/1471-2105-12-323","biotools:rsem","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btp692"],"license":"GPL-3","summary":"We present a generative statistical model and associated inference methods that handle read mapping uncertainty in a principled manner. through simulations parameterized by real rnaseq data, we show that our method is more accurate than previous methods. our improved accuracy is the result ofhandling read mapping uncertainty with a statistical model and the estimationof gene expression levels as the sum of isoform expression levels.","home_url":"http://deweylab.github.io/RSEM/","keywords":["Animals","Base Sequence","Computational Biology","Databases, Genetic","Gene Expression","Gene Expression Profiling","Genome","Mice","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Zea mays","RNA-Seq"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":9241},"biotools":{"id":"rsem","home":"http://deweylab.github.io/RSEM/","summary":"We present a generative statistical model and associated inference methods that handle read mapping uncertainty in a principled manner. Through simulations parameterized by real RNASeq data, we show that our method is more accurate than previous methods. Our improved accuracy is the result of handling read mapping uncertainty with a statistical model and the estimation of gene expression levels as the sum of isoform expression levels.","addition_date":"2017-01-13T13:16:10Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T15:03:29.661059Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rsem","credit":[{"email":"bli25@berkeley.edu","name":"Bo Li","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://bli25ucb.github.io/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://deweylab.github.io/RSEM/README.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"RNA-Seq quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3800"}]}],"name":"RSEM","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"seqwiki_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btp692","pmcid":"PMC2820677","pmid":"20022975"}],"topic":[{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"RSEM","home":"https://bio.tools/rsem","summary":"We present a generative statistical model and associated inference methods that handle read mapping uncertainty in a principled manner. Through simulations parameterized by real RNASeq data, we show that our method is more accurate than previous methods. Our improved accuracy is the result of handling read mapping uncertainty with a statistical model and the estimation of gene expression levels as the sum of isoform expression levels.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rsem/cmd/deweylab.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":false,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":690,"citations":[{"count":10,"year":"2010"},{"count":19,"year":"2026"},{"count":21,"year":"2012"},{"count":23,"year":"2014"},{"count":31,"year":"2011"},{"count":31,"year":"2025"},{"count":32,"year":"2013"},{"count":35,"year":"2024"},{"count":37,"year":"2023"},{"count":45,"year":"2015"},{"count":48,"year":"2016"},{"count":51,"year":"20